<title>UK: Copper whips back up to $2,400, spreads borrowed.</title>
<headline>Copper whips back up to $2,400, spreads borrowed.</headline>
<text>
<p>COPPER - Works back up to $2,400 level, partly recovering from mid-morning sell-off. Borrowing off July helps stabilise market, although spread rates stil softer.</p>
<p>ALUMINIUM - Steady, ably defends $1,600 level.</p>
<p>NICKEL - Steadier near $6,900. TIN - Drifts back.</p>
<p>ZINC - Steady in tight range. LEAD - Pushes above $630.</p>
</text>
